===Etymology===
From {{etyl|yue|en}} {{term|鬼佬||tr=gweilo|lang=yue}}, from {{term|鬼||lang=yue|[[ghost]]}} + {{term|佬||lang=yue|[[guy]], [[fucker]]}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|gweilo}}

# {{context|colloquial|ethnic slur|lang=en}} A [[white]] [[person]] in [[China]], {{context|particularly}} ''of men''; a ‘[[foreign]] [[devil]]’.
#*'''1977''', {{w|John Le Carré}}, ''The Honourable Schoolboy'', Folio Society 2010, p. 179:
#*:She had ruffled the bed and laid a frilly nightdress on the floor because so far as the block was concerned Phoebe was the half-'''''kwailo''''' bastard who whored with the fat foreign devil.

====Usage notes====
Some Caucasians living in [[w:Hong Kong|Hong Kong]] now occasionally use the English '''gweilo''' to jokingly refer to themselves.

